# Prettier must not touch the prose corpus, and the reason is measured rather than stylistic.
#
# 1. It cannot produce house style. The corpus writes emphasis as *emphasis*; Prettier rewrites it
#    to _emphasis_ and has NO option to stop it — verified against the installed 3.7.4, whose
#    markdown options are printWidth, proseWrap, tabWidth, useTabs, endOfLine and the pragma pair.
#    Emphasis style is deliberately not configurable upstream.
#
# 2. Its table padding is destructive here. Prettier pads every cell in a column to the width of the
#    widest cell. `plans/0000-board.md` has a 4,166-character cell, so formatting it takes the file
#    from 82,450 to 182,405 bytes — +100 KB, almost all of it trailing spaces — and every short cell
#    in that column becomes four thousand blanks.
#
# House style is enforced instead by tests/Borough.Tests/Corpus/MarkdownStyleTests.cs, which checks
# the two things that have actually gone wrong rather than reformatting the file.

*.md
